# News/Media Workflow

## Scheduling and Idempotency

- Keep full pipeline cron at `00:00 daily` in `cron/Dockerfile` for all configured scholar IDs.
- Keep `--refresh-news` at `05:00 daily` and `--bake-media-filtered` at `12:00 daily`.
- Keep `FRESH_DATA_SECONDS` aligned with daily full runs (default `82800`, ~23h) so midnight cron performs a real full scrape.

## Scrape and Serve Contract

- `main.py` and `--refresh-news` must write `media` and `media_filtered` (plus `media_filtered_at`) into `scholar_data/<id>.json`.
- `/scholar/<id>/news` in `src/serve.py` should serve `media_filtered` when present; fallback filtering of raw `media` is legacy-only behavior.
- Keep filtering strict for Dr Jodie Rummer relevance; avoid broadening rules that increase false positives.

## Caching and Reprocessing

- Preserve page-HTML cache behavior in `src/news_filters.py`: only cache successful `2xx` HTML fetches; do not cache blocked/captcha/non-2xx responses.
- During fresh news ingestion, skip URLs already indexed in existing `media_filtered` to avoid re-scraping known items.
- Keep URL normalization/dedup logic stable (tracking params removed, source-priority dedupe retained).

## Change Hygiene

- If cron cadence, freshness window, filtering, or serving behavior changes, update both `README.md` and `.env.template` in the same change.
- Maintain tests that cover: daily scheduling assumptions, `media_filtered` precedence, snippet gate behavior, and existing-URL skip behavior.
